      "created_at": "2020-12-16T16:47:02Z",
      "updated_at": "2020-12-16T16:47:02Z",
      "body": "This is a direct GDPR requirement. +1 on breaking this up into 2 \nseparate requirements or turn OR into AND. PR us!\n\n- Jim\n\nOn 12/16/20 2:53 AM, Sjoerd Langkemper wrote:\n>\n> Verify that users have a method to remove *or* export their data on \n> demand. \n> <https://github.com/OWASP/ASVS/blob/master/4.0/en/0x16-V8-Data-Protection.md>\n>\n> There are two requirements here:\n>\n>   * users must be able to export their data\n>   * users must be able to remove their data\n>\n> The way this requirement is currently stated allows implementors to \n> choose either of these. I don't think that makes sense. Export and \n> removal do not solve the same problem.\n>\n> The \"method\" this requirements mentions can also be to email the \n> support desk, it doesn't have to be integrated in the application, in \n> my opinion. In that case, does this even belong in the ASVS? What is \n> the application's role in this? Should every application have export \n> functionality built in? Should every application have functionality to \n> remove data built in?\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you are subscribed to this thread.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub \n> <https://github.com/OWASP/ASVS/issues/883>, or unsubscribe \n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AAEBYCIS3SDT5IX2CA246NLSVCUWJANCNFSM4U56BRYA>.\n>\n-- \nJim Manico\nManicode Security\nhttps://www.manicode.com\n\n",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
