      "created_at": "2021-03-18T15:37:57Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-03-18T15:37:57Z",
      "body": "The GDPR says users have a right to [receive](https://gdpr.eu/article-20-right-to-data-portability/) or [delete](https://gdpr.eu/article-17-right-to-be-forgotten/) their data. However, it doesn't say that this functionality should be present in the application. Technically, neither does the ASVS:\r\n\r\n> Verify that users have a method to remove or export their data on demand.\r\n\r\nIs it sufficient if I could call the help desk and a database administrator deletes some rows from the database? If so, does this belong in the ASVS? This seems to be more a business process verification than an application verification.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
